                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{F}
                is a continuously differentiable vector field on a neighbourhood of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+lemma"} Poincaré lemma
            %li
              %p
                %strong Stokes theorem
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+Stokes+theorem"} nonabelian Stokes theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+theorem"} de Rham theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+theorem"} Hodge theorem
            %li
              %p
                a special case is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy%27s+integral+theorem"} Cauchy's integral theorem
          %h2#References References
          %p The basic statement:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raoul+Bott"}> Raoul Bott
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loring+Tu"} Loring Tu
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Differential+Forms+in+Algebraic+Topology"} Differential Forms in Algebraic Topology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-3951-0"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-3951-0
          %p
            In the generality of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds+with+corners"} manifolds with corners
          %ul
            %li#Lee12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Lee"}> John Lee
                , Theorem 10.32 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to Smooth Manifolds
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4419-9982-5"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4419-9982-5
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://lost-contact.mit.edu/afs/adrake.org/usr/rkh/Books/books/Introduction%20to%20Smooth%20Manifolds%20-%20J.%20Lee.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+Conrad"}> Brian Conrad
                \:
                %em Stokes’ theorem with corners
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://math.stanford.edu/~conrad/diffgeomPage/handouts/stokescorners.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/ConradStokesTheorem.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Statement of the fiberwise Stokes theorem:
          %ul
            %li#GomiTerashima00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kiyonori+Gomi"}> Kiyonori Gomi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuji+Terashima"} Yuji Terashima
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Fiber Integration Formula for the Smooth Deligne Cohomology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://imrn.oxfordjournals.org/content/2000/13/699.full.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://numr.wdfiles.com/local--files/differential-cohomology/gomi-terashima.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1155/S1073792800000386"} doi:10.1155/S1073792800000386
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liviu+Nicolaescu"}> Liviu Nicolaescu
                , Theorem 3.4.54 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on the Geometry of Manifolds
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www3.nd.edu/~lnicolae/Lectures.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/NicolaescuGeometryOfManifolds.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p and specifically for simplicial differential forms:
          %ul
            %li
              Dupont, Ljungman, Theorem 5.10 in:
              %em Integration of simllicial forms and Deligne cohomology
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0402059"}> arXiv:math/0402059
              )
          %p
            Statement of the Stokes theorem in the full generality of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} fiberwise integration
            over fibers
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold+with+corners"} with corners
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Cattaneo"}> Alberto Cattaneo
              , Nima Moshayedi, Konstantin Wernli, equation (65) in:
              %em Globalization for Perturbative Quantization of Nonlinear Split AKSZ Sigma Models on Manifolds with Boundary
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.11782"}> arXiv:1807.11782
              )
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chains"} chains
            of smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplices"} singular simplices
          %ul
            %li
              %em Stokes’ theorem on chains
              (
              %a{:href => "http://idv.sinica.edu.tw/ftliang/diff_geom/*diff_geometry(II)/3.25/deRham_theorem/stokes_on_chains.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p Discussion for manifolds with more general singularities on the boundary is in
          %ul
            %li
              Friedrich Sauvigny,
              %em Partial Differential Equations: Vol. 1 Foundations and Integral Representations
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} cohesive homotopy type theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"} Thomas Nikolaus
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+V%C3%B6lkl"} Michael Völkl
              %em Differential cohomology theories as sheaves of spectra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.3188"}> arXiv:1311.3188
              )
